---
source: tests/golden/notifications.rs
expression: "norm::text(&out)"
---
provider: ntfy (ntfy)

## minimal config
{
  "priority": "auto",
  "server": "https://ntfy.sh",
  "topic": "vigilant-alerts"
}

### down
POST https://ntfy.sh/
(json)
{
  "click": "https://vv.example/monitors/7",
  "message": "HTTP 503 (after 3 retries)\nTarget: https://pay.example/health\nType: HTTP(S)\nTime: 2026-10-19 14:03:12 UTC\nhttps://vv.example/monitors/7",
  "priority": 5,
  "tags": [
    "red_circle"
  ],
  "title": "Payments API is down",
  "topic": "vigilant-alerts"
}

### up
POST https://ntfy.sh/
(json)
{
  "click": "https://vv.example/monitors/7",
  "message": "down for 12m 4s\nTarget: https://pay.example/health\nType: HTTP(S)\nDowntime: 12m 4s\nTime: 2026-10-19 14:03:12 UTC\nhttps://vv.example/monitors/7",
  "priority": 3,
  "tags": [
    "green_circle"
  ],
  "title": "Payments API is back up",
  "topic": "vigilant-alerts"
}

## full config
{
  "access_token": "tk_",
  "password": "secret-password",
  "priority": "auto",
  "server": "https://ntfy.sh",
  "tags": "prod, payments",
  "topic": "vigilant-alerts",
  "username": "username-value"
}

### down
POST https://ntfy.sh/
Authorization: Bearer tk_
(json)
{
  "click": "https://vv.example/monitors/7",
  "message": "HTTP 503 (after 3 retries)\nTarget: https://pay.example/health\nType: HTTP(S)\nTime: 2026-10-19 14:03:12 UTC\nhttps://vv.example/monitors/7",
